# Pachim commands

When the user must run something on Pachim (دستورات / SSH panel):

- One command per block. Never chain with `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|`, or newlines in one paste.
- Each command must be under 255 characters.
- Do not wrap multiple steps in a one-liner. Number them: run 1, wait, then 2.
- Prefer simple `cp`, `mv`, `git checkout HEAD -- path`, `git pull origin main`.
- RTL replies: keep these command blocks LTR and separate from Persian sentences.
- If a git pathspec fails, use `git checkout HEAD -- path` not `git checkout -- path`.
